{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And on that day I will set apart the land of Goshen</b> — Since the earlier plagues were localized, it is no wonder that they were in the land of Egypt and not in the land of Goshen. But this is a sent plague, and when the beasts come up from their dens — lions from the mountains, leopards from the hills — and ravage all the land of Egypt, it would be in their nature that they also come into the land of Goshen, which is part of the land of Egypt within it. Therefore it was necessary to say <b>and I will set apart the land of Goshen</b>, that it would be entirely delivered for the sake of <b>for My people stands upon it</b>, for the majority of Israel is there. And He says <b>and I will put a redemption between My people and your people</b>, that even in the land of Egypt, if the beasts find a Jewish man they will not harm him, but they will devour the Egyptians, as it is written (Psalms 78:45), \"He sent among them swarms and they devoured them.\" And this is the meaning of <b>redemption</b> — in the sense of \"I gave men in exchange for you, Egypt, Cush and Seba under you\" (Isaiah 43:3):" "<b>For I am YHWH in the midst of the land</b> — Ibn Ezra (on Exodus 8:18) explained it by way of parable, like the custom of kings who station themselves in the middle of the kingdom so as to be near the borders. And this has no reason. Rather, it is to say that He rules and exercises providence <b>in the midst of the land</b> — not like one who thinks \"Thick clouds are a covering to Him, that He sees not; and He walks in the circuit of heaven\" (Job 22:14). And it is possible that it is like \"for My name is in his midst\" (Exodus 23:21), and this is a supernal and hidden secret:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Ramban quotes Isaiah 43:3 using only its opening words נָתַתִּי כָפְרְךָ מִצְרַיִם כּוּשׁ וּסְבָא תַּחְתֶּיךָ; I supplied the fuller clause with the standard prophetic context for the word כָפֶר as a ransom-substitute, matching Ramban's analogy to פְדוּת."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:55.781665730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}